APOLLO, Logistics (the hauler- ships)
Order: keep the fleet's goods, sell what stands in storage, and make the tool the miners lack. At 02:49 UTC all 20 of your ships wait. Beside the harvester chain, the gas routes Trade has not taken are yours to test, one hauler each (a Gas Harvester stands at 1,202 cr at Node Beta); your Standing Plan names what your haulers fly between two turns. (1) The 302 stored soma sell into station bids near 650 cr that refill within the hour (your report of 23:58 UTC): sell them where they lie as the pools refill, by hand until the runner sells from storage (owed, requests.log ENT-065). (2) The harvester chain (GOAL): the tool catalog with ask=item prints every recipe of the harvester and of each input; ask=needs follows one recipe only. Make one harvester by hand with one hauler: steel plate and circuit boards from the stored ore, flex polymer bought (from 129 cr) or made, a power cell from 2 circuit boards, 3 energy crystals and 2 copper wiring. Say what it cost in credits and minutes and whether a skill or a workshop bounds it. One made is the test; ten are the fleet's first supply chain (strategy, phase 2). (3) Your haulers earn meanwhile with what pays in the fleet: the missions that pay once (First Steps is on again, ENT-064), the Node Beta chain with Mercury's word, the ice routes with Zero's word and a harvester each; fill with action=status and who=hauler names what is open and what closes the rest. (4) Keep the silicon ore and the energy crystal at Central Nexus for circuit boards (your suggestion, accepted). The storage home and the lockbox stand as you reported them. (5) Capacity (F18): what storage holds and what it can be made into today (the tool catalog, ask=can), what that would sell for, and how many haulers the fleet's hauling needs.
